ants /Library/Keychains read+write to any com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension holder, and 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No value, no portal capability, no new App ID, no C1 change. FIELD-BY-FIELD (all five keys on the row): status prohibited-pending-decision -> prohibited; rationale -> the settled reason above citing TASK-260728-7ii1xz; evidence -> keep and add application.sb:792-793 plus checks E8-E10; resolutionOwner -> REMOVE (this task IS the resolution; a settled row naming a pending resolver reads as still-open); amendmentRule -> REMOVE and replace with M5. The amendmentRule removal is the critical one: its antecedent (transport gives the provider direct keychain access) is now TRUE while its consequent (amend to required with the group literal) is FALSE, so left in place it is a live instruction to re-grant the row on exactly the reasoning this decision refutes. M2: close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz as resolver. M3: keep OC-4 open, downgraded to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected. M4: macos.host keychain-access-groups - no change requested, recommend keep granted with the purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus a macOS pre-seed staging item. M5: record the replacement rule - on macOS the file-based keychain is SecAccess-ACL controlled and keychain-access-groups applies only to the Data Protection Keychain, so a root-context provider never needs it and the presence of the key in a shipping third-party provider is not evidence it functions; the row reopens only if the provider is ever moved into a user context. M6: application-groups on both macOS targets - no value change, but the stated purpose and the section 10 traceability row implying a shared container on macOS are FALSE (host and provider resolve different containers). M7: bump revision, append a revisionLog entry naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz_reviewer-verdict-01.md and this decision, keep validate-matrix at exit 0, and check that deleting resolutionOwner/amendmentRule does not trip an exhaustive containment assertion - if one requires them it encoded the open state and must be updated in the same revision. Consider a negative gate: a prohibited row still carrying a resolutionOwner is a contradiction. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.
