Accepted. `TASK-260728-7ii1xz` is now `done`.

The selected transport is a provider-owned, system-domain file-based keychain item seeded through the NE app-message channel. This aligns with Apple’s [macOS keychain model](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/technotes/tn3137-on-mac-keychains), [message lifecycle contract](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/networkextension/netunnelprovidersession/sendprovidermessage(_:responsehandler:)), and [DTS guidance](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/759976).

Entitlement verdict:

- `works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel` keeps `keychain-access-groups` prohibited, with no value or portal capability.
- `resolutionOwner` and the stale `amendmentRule` must be removed by `TASK-260715-ypo7yo`.
- Both macOS targets retain App Group literal `group.works.relux.tunnel`, but it is not described as a shared file container.

Verified gates:

- `swift test`: exit 0 — 335 tests in 29 suites.
- Keychain probe compile/run: exit 0.
- Physical evidence collector: exit 0; expected root-container check recorded exit 1.
- Final `task-board validate`: exit 0 — no issues found.

